# Frontend - Welfare Database Management System

## Environment Configuration

Create a `.env` file in the frontend directory:

```env
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1
REACT_APP_APP_NAME=Welfare DB System
```

## Installation

```bash
npm install
```

## Development

```bash
npm start
```

The application will open at `http://localhost:3000`

## Build

```bash
npm run build
```

## Testing

```bash
npm test
```

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/          # Reusable React components
│   ├── Common/         # Header, Sidebar, etc.
│   ├── Forms/          # Form components
│   └── Tables/         # Data table components
├── pages/              # Page components
│   ├── Dashboard/
│   ├── Members/
│   ├── Dependants/
│   ├── Payments/
│   ├── Reports/
│   └── Auth/
├── services/           # API calls
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
├── store/              # State management (Zustand)
├── styles/             # Global styles
├── utils/              # Utility functions
├── App.js              # Main App component
└── index.js            # React entry point
```

## Features

- **Authentication**: Login and registration with JWT
- **Dashboard**: Overview of key metrics
- **Member Management**: CRUD operations for members
- **Dependant Management**: Track member dependants and benefits
- **Payment Tracking**: Record and verify payments
- **Reporting**: Generate financial and membership reports
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly UI with Material-UI

## Key Components

### Authentication Pages
- Login page
- Registration page
- Password reset

### Main Pages
- Dashboard with metrics and charts
- Members list and detail pages
- Dependants management
- Payments tracking
- Reports generation

### Common Components
- Navigation sidebar
- Header with user menu
- Confirmation dialogs
- Loading states
- Error boundaries

## API Integration

All API calls are centralized in the `services/` directory:

```javascript
import { memberService } from './services/api';

// Get all members
const members = await memberService.getAll();

// Create member
await memberService.create(memberData);

// Update member
await memberService.update(id, memberData);

// Delete member
await memberService.delete(id);
```

## State Management

Using Zustand for state management:

```javascript
import { useStore } from './store';

const user = useStore((state) => state.user);
const setUser = useStore((state) => state.setUser);
```

## Styling

- Material-UI for components
- CSS-in-JS with Emotion
- Custom theme configuration

## Forms

- Formik for form management
- Yup for validation
- Custom form components

## Data Visualization

- Recharts for charts and graphs
- Custom dashboard widgets

## Performance

- React Query for server state management
- Lazy loading of routes
- Memoization of expensive components

